vote":"aye"},{"name":"Skye Kakoschke-Moore","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10854","person_slug":"skye-kakoschke-moore","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stirling Griff","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10851","person_slug":"stirling-griff","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Census - Do not fine","noes":41,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2016-09-12.125.1) introduced by [Scott Ludlam](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/wa/scott_ludlam), which means it was unsuccessful. The motion called for no Australians to be fined for not completing the census in light of the [technical failures](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2016-08-09/abs-website-inaccessible-on-census-night/7711652) and [privacy concerns](http://www.abc.net.au/btn/story/s4517867.htm). ### Motion text > *That the Senate—* > *(a) notes:* >> *(i) the [technical failures](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2016-08-09/abs-website-inaccessible-on-census-night/7711652) of the [Australian Bureau of Statistics](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_Bureau_of_Statistics) (ABS) website on [Census](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Census_in_Australia) night, 9 August 2016, prevented thousands of people completing the Census,* >> *(ii) subsequent attempts to address the technical failures further added to confusion and impacted public confidence in the Census process,* >> *(iii) the Census website was offline for several days after census night, and sporadically offline in the following weeks, and* >> *(iv) thousands of Australians were unable to complete the Census, and thousands of Australians were reluctant to do so due to [privacy concerns](http://www.abc.net.au/btn/story/s4517867.htm); and* > *(b) calls on the Government to direct the ABS to issue a statement declaring that no Australians will be fined for failing to complete the Census.*","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4286","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-09-12/5"}
